      <h2 class="resume-block__heading">Professional Summary</h2>
      <p class="resume-block__prose">Principal engineer and security architect with 23 years across operations, networking, SRE, software, and security. Most recently I led security architecture and agentic engineering at InspectionGo, after nearly 15 years at GoDaddy building production security platforms, control planes, and policy-driven infrastructure across data centers and clouds, security engineering at IBM, and signal operations in the U.S. Army. My research focuses on securing inference and agent execution through explicit authority, isolation, secret custody, and evidence provenance.</p>
      <p class="resume-block__prose">Proficient in more than a dozen languages and fluent in many of them, I work across the full depth of the stack. I learn fast, with a track record of adopting unfamiliar technologies and delivering production systems within weeks. I favor small, composable interfaces, minimal coupling, clear ownership boundaries, and code that communicates its intent without requiring a tour guide. I build systems that enable experimentation without turning production into a casino.</p>
